  },
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "information",
      "topic": "Fixed represented code",
      "finding": "The two-parameter PR blueprint defines prefix(n+1,B,Bprime)=conj(weq(B[n],Bprime[n]),prefix(n,B,Bprime)); base code0 is truth. EqCtx uses the left internal vector length. The explicit Sigma1 graphs and Delta1 total-function interfaces avoid treating an external Lean list as an arbitrary internal conjunction."
    },
    {
      "severity": "information",
      "topic": "Induction strength",
      "finding": "prefix_projection uses a bounded family of Sigma1 proof witnesses; prefix_cons_equiv uses two Sigma1 proof witnesses with environments fixed. I-Sigma1 induction is appropriate for both. No universal-environment proof-existence induction is claimed at Pi1."
    },
    {
      "severity": "information",
      "topic": "Finite propositional steps",
      "finding": "conj_intro_imp applies the assumed implication a\u2192(b\u2192false) to a and b, then discharges it. conj_under, right monotonicity and conjunction interchange follow by the checked finite projections. The cons equivalence transports the head equality through the reverse conjunction using this interchange; both directions have the correct order."
    },
    {
      "severity": "information",
      "topic": "Binder interface",
      "finding": "discharge_cons discharges old context first, then new weq(x,y), exactly producing the curried body premise needed by all_relational. under_cons reverses this. all_of_cons preserves all four explicit Vac resources; it does not assert that they follow automatically."
    },
    {
      "severity": "information",
      "topic": "Stack lengths and lookup",
      "finding": "EqCtx, projection and cons laws are total and deliberately require no equal-length assumption. When interpreting EqCtx as correspondence between two bound stacks, the downstream encoder invariant must supply both depths. For ordinary Avoid-based context vacuity, equal lengths are needed to transport the right-stack avoidance range; prefix-vacuity can instead state both ranges explicitly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "information",
      "topic": "Remaining alpha obligations",
      "finding": "This module does not construct formula transport, cross-body Vac witnesses, equality substitution, global accepted-proof renaming or proof compilation. Formula induction and the four vacuity premises remain the downstream alpha task. No circular use of any such conclusion appears in the source."
    }
  ],
